  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Online Bureau\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Updated On Sep 1, 2026 at 02:16 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                            <li>\n                                                        \n                                                            \n                                                                Read by \n                                                            \n                                                            100 Professionals\n                                                        \n                                                    </li>\n                                                                                    </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: <a href=\"/tag/max+healthcare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Max Healthcare</a> is set to enter Gujarat with a 800 bed multi-speciality hospital, <a href=\"/tag/chief+minister+bhupendra+patel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chief Minister Bhupendra Patel</a> said in a post on social media platform X.The announcement was made following Patel’s meeting with Abhay Soi, Chairman and Managing Director of Max Healthcare in Delhi.Patel added that the healthcare major is also planning future expansion across Gandhinagar and Surat.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>“Discussed Max Healthcare’s plans to enter Gujarat's healthcare sector starting with a modern 800-bed multi-specialty hospital, alongside future expansion across Gandhinagar and Surat. They appreciated Gujarat’s progressive urban planning and favorable FSI policies that encourage large-scale healthcare infrastructure.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>“Gujarat remains committed to building world-class medical facilities and strengthening our healthcare ecosystem to provide top-tier care for all,” Patel said.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The healthcare major currently operates 21 healthcare facilities with over 6100 across the NCR Delhi, Haryana, Punjab, Uttarakhand, Maharashtra and Odisha, with plans to reach a total of 10,000 beds over the next three to four years.In the first quarter ended June this year, Max reported a 16 per cent year-on-year (YoY) rise in gross revenue to Rs 2,982 crore.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Its network PAT grew 3 per cent YoY to Rs 357 crore, compared to Rs 345 crore in Q1 FY26.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                        